  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Convolution and State",
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "The Q/K/V convolution has a per-request window cache retaining the last three projected inputs. Requests must not share convolution history.",
        "Interpret the recurrent state with value rows and key columns: decay key channels, predict the current V, write only the error, then read with Q.",
        "Prefill can use a chunk algorithm and decode an incremental recurrence. Edges show mathematical dependencies, not kernel launches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Three Distinct Gates",
      "dot": "amber",
      "items": [
        "Beta controls write strength; alpha is retention per key channel; z gates the normalized output with sigmoid.",
        "The state here has all 64 heads. At TP=8 the tutorial has 8 heads per rank and state [8,128,128]."
      ]
    }
  ]
